leuk                 package:AA                      R Documentation

Survival Times and White Blood Cell Counts

Description:

     The 'leuk' data frame has 17 rows and 2 columns.

     Survival times in weeks of 17 patients with leukaemia, along with
     their base 10 logarithm of the white blood cell counts at the time
     of diagnosis.

Usage:

     data(leuk)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'x' the logarithm (base 10) of the white blood cell counts for
          each patient;

     't' the survival time in weeks of leukaemia patients.

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Feigl, P. and Zelen, M. (1965).  Estimation of exponential
     survival probabilities with concomitant information. 
     _Biometrics_, *21*, 826-838.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Example 5.5.

     Cox, D.R. and Snell, E.J. (1981).  _Applied Statistics: Principles
     and Examples_.  Chapman & Hall, London.  Example U.

Examples:

     data(leuk)
     plot(t ~ x, data = leuk, xlab = "white blood cell counts", 
          ylab = "survival time")
